This is because the original intention was to provide a damage bonus,
depending on the amount of stored energy. This way, a +0 wizard staff
is a lousy weapon, but excellent to store energy; at +5, it is a good
weapon but bad for storing energy. I don't implement the damage bonus
code yet because I'm not sure what is the best way to do it.
Thinking about it now and re-reading the old post that suggested this
idea, I think the best way to do both and avoiding (much) unbalance is
making it so some of the energy is lost, when storing/using or when
attacking with the staff. Hmmm...

> adding >100 points to a wizard's mp maximum seems unbalancing to me.

I'm not really sure I understood what you meant here. You're saying
'adding points to mp maximum' because when the wizard's energy is
depleted he actually have more in the staff? If this is what you
meant, making it lose part of its charge maybe would balance it. And
if the wizard don't want to use the staff as his primary weapon, the
nuisance of having to change weapons to use the stored energy could
make it less appealing...

And, yes, I agree that at this point and even with these changes it
is/can be unbalancing; I'm just toying with the idea of having some
kind of magical staff. Maybe the wizard role already have much energy
at his disposal, but wouldn't it be nice if other roles have some sort
of energy enhancing? Think of a priest or a caveman (who can be expert
at staves) using one of these.

